      "id": "P1",
      "text": "COLONOSCOPY REPORT"
    },
    {
      "id": "P2",
      "text": "Date of service: November 9, 2026"
    },
    {
      "id": "P3",
      "text": "Endoscopist: A. Current, MD (fictional)"
    },
    {
      "id": "P4",
      "text": "Indication: Colorectal anastomotic stricture after a sigmoid colectomy in 2023; straining and narrow stools."
    },
    {
      "id": "P5",
      "text": "HISTORY"
    },
    {
      "id": "P6",
      "text": "A colonoscopy in March 2024 found the anastomosis narrowed but passable."
    },
    {
      "id": "P7",
      "text": "No dilation was carried out in 2024."
    },
    {
      "id": "P8",
      "text": "The colonoscope was advanced to the colorectal anastomosis at 20 cm, where a short benign-appearing stricture admitted the scope only with resistance."
    },
    {
      "id": "P9",
      "text": "A through-the-scope balloon was passed across the stricture and inflated to 15 mm for 60 seconds."
    },
    {
      "id": "P10",
      "text": "The colonoscope then passed easily and was advanced to the cecum; the appendiceal orifice and ileocecal valve were identified."
    },
    {
      "id": "P11",
      "text": "Colorectal anastomotic stricture dilated with a through-the-scope balloon to 15 mm."
    }
  ],
